                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1567-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_xy.png" width=27 height=27 alt="X/Y Stereo" title="X/Y Stereo" ></span>R&#00216;DE iXY</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    X/Y Stereo Condenser Stereo Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The iXY is a stereo recording solution for the iOS market. It is available in two versions, the iXY-30PIN for 30-pin connectors, and, as of 2014, the iXY-L for the lightning connector.</p><p>It is the first 24-bit ADC mic solution for the iPhone. </p><p>The iXY consists of two prepolarized half-inch condenser capsules in a fixed 90&deg; XY array. The housing is metal, contributing both ruggedness and EMI shielding. </p><p>A proprietary onboard ADC does analog to digital conversion at up to 24 bits of resolution, at a maximum sample rate of 96 kHz. The iPhone&#8217;s dock connector accepts the digital audio stream without additional conversion. </p><p>Rode&#8217;s &#8220;Rode Rec&#8221; app, available via the App Store, comes in two versions. The free &#8220;LE&#8221; version offers basic mono or stereo recording (at up to 24/96), and export in multiple audio formats via FTP or SoundCloud. The full version (priced at $5.99 as of January 2013) offers additional output formats, editing, compression, and Dropbox integration. Both versions of the app can be used with the device&#8217;s built-in microphone, with the iXY, or with other 3rd-party microphone systems such as the Blue Mikey Digital.</p><p><a rel="shadowbox" href="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images//mic_extras/rode/iXY.jpg"><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/rode/iXY_sm.jpg" class="thumb shaft" alt="Rode iXY" width="220" /></a><em>Is the iXY compatible with the Apple Lightning connector?</em> </p><p>According to RODE tech support, the iXY was tested extensively with the 30-pin to Lightning adapter. Officially, this usage is <a href="http://www.rodemic.com/faq/ixy-and-lightning-compatibility">not recommended</a>, presumably because cantilevering the 40g weight of the iXY at the end of the adapter creates a recording device that is not as stable or secure as the iXY was designed to be. </p><p>The mic unit ships with a foam windscreen and a form-fitting storage pouch. It has no physical buttons or switches; all configuration is done via the Rode Rec app for iPhone/iPad.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Rode/iXY">R&#00216;DE iXY</a></p><p>The mic was released in 2013.</p>
